WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.910
Christopher Nolan's movies often require a
repeat screening or two to fully process all

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:08.840
the plot layers and subtle details, and Inception
is no different.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.660
The 2010 film — which thrusts its leads
into a chemically-induced dream state where

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:18.939
they attempt to implant ideas into people's
minds — was so complex and ambiguous that

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:23.100
the director's true meaning has become a point
of cinematic controversy.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.380
Don't worry, though, we've got your back.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:32.620
Let's dive into explaining the ending of Inception.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.580
Grief and guilt

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.740
At its core, Inception is about two things:
grief and guilt.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:43.160
Leonardo DiCaprio's Cobb is working to get
back to his children after his wife Mal committed

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:46.960
self harm — which looks more like Cobb himself
killed her.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.180
At least that's how he remembers it.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:52.320
but his memories are clouded by guilt, over his role in her passing.

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:56.740
After an experiment gone wrong, which trapped
Mal and Cobb together for what seemed like

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:01.780
decades in limbo, Mal became so absorbed in
the dream world that she could no longer tell

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.400
the difference between different layers of
existence.

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:09.060
In her mind, the waking world was just another
layer she needed to kick herself out of.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:13.460
So when she leaped from a high rise hotel,
she didn't think she'd actually harm herself.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:18.080
Cobb feels so responsible for Mal's passing
that he keeps his sharpest memories of her

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.340
locked away in his mind.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:25.439
But when his protégé Ariadne releases Mind-Mal
into the dream, she becomes his biggest obstacle

00:01:25.439 --> 00:01:29.630
in completing his inception mission for Mr.
Saito: she creeps into the third

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:33.700
layer of the group mission and sends their
target, Robert Fischer, into Limbo.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:38.520
Cobb eventually realizes Mind-Mal is just
a projection of his guilt and grief and let's

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:39.880
Ariadne "kill" her.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:44.220
That theme of getting through a difficult
loss like this plays out on a parallel plane

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:48.520
with Robert Fischer, as he's basically guided
through the five stages of grief amid the

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:49.800
looming death of his dad.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:54.820
In the end Cobb decides to embrace the reality
he's currently in with his children.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.540
In doing so, he also lets go of his guilt
and grief.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:04.640
It's probably no coincidence that Nolan lost
his own father in 2009, suggesting that Inception

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:07.180
may just be his most personal film ever.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:13.400
"Chris is very expressive in what he's trying
to accomplish but it is insulated in his own

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.680
mind so we knew we had to take a leap of faith."

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:18.600
That darn top!

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:23.360
The biggest question viewers have after seeing
Inception is this: will the spinning top at

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:24.700
the end ever fall down?

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:29.880
The top was a totem Cobb had created to show
whether or not he was in a dream or in true

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:34.490
reality — in a dream, it would spin forever,
but in the real world, it would eventually

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:35.180
fall over.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:40.010
For Nolan, though, the whole point of that
ending is that it doesn't matter to Cobb anymore

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:44.090
whether he's in a dream world or the real
world, which is why he doesn't bother waiting

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:46.160
to find out the results of his final spin.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:50.771
He's happy to be reunited with his children,
and he decides that this is the reality he

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:54.610
wants to live in regardless of whether it's
a dream or not.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:57.360
"We all dream, it's a, it's a universal experience.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:59.100
Uh, but a very private one."

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.040
It's all Greek to us

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:06.540
In Greek mythology, Ariadne is a young goddess
on the island of Crete who's put in charge

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.620
of a labyrinth that sees the sacrifice of
several Athenians each year.

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:16.000
But upon finding affection for one of its
would-be victims, Theseus, she helps him escape

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:21.150
by giving him a red string and a sword to
defeat the Minotaur and find his way out of

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:21.820
the maze.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:28.360
Not only does Inception's Ariadne almost always
wear red, but she also slowly but surely shows

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:33.440
Cobb the way to overcome his own demon: the
long-lingering image of his deceased wife.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:39.020
Some fans theorize Ariadne may have originally
been hired by Stephen Miles, Mal's father,

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.780
to discover whether Cobb had actually killed
Mal or was as innocent as he claimed.

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:48.940
That would explain why Ariadne is so acutely
interested in delving into Cobb and Mal's

00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:49.440
history.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:53.980
After seeing the toll it takes on him, however,
she may have developed a fondness or sympathy

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:59.680
for him and decides to help him "escape" in
the end, much like her mythological namesake.

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:01.280
Daddy issues

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:06.040
Cobb &amp; Co. have to sift through a lot of layers
to get to the bottom of Fischer's allegiance

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:10.680
to his father's company, but by the end, it
becomes clear that all Fischer ever really

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:13.940
wanted was the affection and respect of his
old man.

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:19.140
That's why, when his dad tells him to open
the safe that'd been planted by Cobb's team

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:24.819
in his dreamworld hospital room, all it contains
was a pinwheel that reminds Fischer of one

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:27.060
of the few happy memories from his childhood.

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:32.020
For Fischer, the pinwheel signifies that his
dad treasured him more than he ever let on,

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:36.780
which gives value to his suggestion that Fischer
go off and become his own man — and thus

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:39.900
dissolve the company that's causing Mr. Saito
so much trouble.

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:42.060
The eye of the needle

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:47.500
While Saito isn't exactly evil, he's willing
to go to some great lengths in order to get

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:52.960
a financial profit for his company, including
literally entering someone else's mind and

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:54.220
planting thoughts in it.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:59.980
But Saito's plan backfires spectacularly when
he dies within the dream and is sent to limbo.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:04.840
Cobb manages to rescue him, but not until
Saito has aged to the point of senility.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:09.780
When they finally emerge from the dream and
back into reality, Saito isn't thrilled about

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:14.550
his financial victory, but instead he's rather
stoic and seems to have experienced a change

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:17.380
of heart as a result of his time in limbo.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:21.819
With both Saito and Fischer, Nolan seems to
be saying there's a lot more to life than

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:26.680
the pursuit of wealth, a theme he would pick
up on in his next film, The Dark Knight Rises.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:29.960
But that's not the only impact Inception would
have on Hollywood.

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:32.780
Inception's Legacy

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:37.580
Not only did the themes of Inception carry
over into The Dark Knight Rises, specific

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:40.580
character arcs did too, as crazy as that sounds.

00:05:40.789 --> 00:05:45.660
Joseph Gordon-Levitt's Inception character
Arthur is tasked with keeping watch over his

00:05:45.669 --> 00:05:51.539
helpless comrades in much the same way that
his Dark Knight Rises character Blake protects

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:53.800
the innocent kids of Gotham City.

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:59.260
Tom Hardy's Bane, meanwhile, picks up where
his Inception character Eames leaves off,

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:02.880
using masks and ultra-violence to achieve
his ends.

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:08.120
And Marion Cotillard's Miranda and Mal are
each so devoted to their convictions that

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:11.880
they don't hesitate to sacrifice themselves
for what they believe in.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:15.460
The end of Inception didn't just affect Nolan's
movies, either.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:22.740
Raking in over $825 million worldwide while
also garnering massive critical acclaim, Inception

00:06:22.741 --> 00:06:28.880
paved the way for a whole wave of high concept,
big budget sci-fi fare, including films like

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:35.740
Looper, Source Code, The Adjustment Bureau,
Limitless, In Time, Edge of Tomorrow, and

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:36.320
Lucy.

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:41.960
And then there's Marvel's Doctor Strange,
which unapologetically lifted Inception's

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:44.240
entire city-bending sequence.

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:49.620
However, the most obvious — and annoying — influence
of Inception, though, may be this.

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:04.780
Created by composer Hans Zimmer to give potency
to several action sequences, this obnoxious

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:09.820
noise has been featured in seemingly every
sci-fi blockbuster since Inception.

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:11.660
And Zimmer hates it.

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:14.120
He told Vulture, "Oh, it's horrible!

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:17.080
This is a perfect example of where it all
goes wrong.

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:20.460
That music became the blueprint for all action
movies, really.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:24.400
And if you get too many imitations, even I
get confused!"

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:27.460
So...All we can say is…

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:29.500
BRRRRAAAAAMMMMMMM!

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:32.500
BRRRRAAAAAMMMMMMM!

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:34.200
(coughing)

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:35.720
Enter the dream

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:40.020
Ever since Inception's debut, fans have been
clamoring for a sequel.

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:45.039
But while Nolan has publicly toyed with the
idea of a video game that allows players to

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:48.440
explore the world of Inception, so far nothing
has come of it.

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:53.300
Still, there's hope that someday, fans may
be able to play through Inception themselves

00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:57.000
and figure out first hand just what the ending
means to them.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:58.180
Thanks for watching!

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:00.820
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:03.260
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

